letions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/pages/router/web/middleware.mdx","lines":["@@ -1,14 +1,15 @@"," ---"," title: Server middleware"," description: Learn how to create middleware that runs for every request to the server in Expo Router.","-isAlpha: true"," ---"," "," import { Collapsible } from '~/ui/components/Collapsible';"," import { Terminal } from '~/ui/components/Snippet';"," import { Step } from '~/ui/components/Step';"," ","-> **important** Server middleware is in [alpha](/more/release-statuses/#alpha) and is available in SDK 54 and later. It requires a [deployed server](/router/web/api-routes/#deployment) for production use.","+> **important** Server middleware is stable in SDK 58 and later. For SDK 54–57, enable `unstable_useServerMiddleware` in the `expo-router` config plugin. Server middleware requires a [deployed server](/router/web/api-routes/#deployment) for production use.","+","+In SDK 58 and later, `unstable_useServerMiddleware` is deprecated and has no effect. Remove it from your config to avoid the deprecation warning."," "," Server middleware in Expo Router allows you to run code before requests reach your routes, enabling powerful server-side functionality like authentication and logging for every request. Unlike [API routes](/router/web/api-routes) that handle specific endpoints, middleware runs for **every** request in your app, so it should run as quickly as possible to avoid slowing down your app's performance. Client-side navigation such as on native, or in a web app when using [`<Link />`](/versions/latest/sdk/router/link/#link), will not move through the server middleware."," ","@@ -30,16 +31,7 @@ First, configure your app to use server output by adding the server configuratio","       \"output\": \"server\"","       /* @end */","     },","-    \"plugins\": [","-      [","-        \"expo-router\",","-        {","-          /* @info Enables server middleware */","-          \"unstable_useServerMiddleware\": true","-          /* @end */","-        }","-      ]","-    ]","+    \"plugins\": [\"expo-router\"]","   }"," }"," ```"],"additions":4,"deletions":12,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/pages/versions/unversioned/sdk/router/index.mdx","lines":["@@ -128,9 +128,9 @@ If you are using the [default](/more/create-expo/#--template) template to create","     {","       name: 'unstable_useServerMiddleware',","       description:","-        'Enable server middleware support with a `+middleware.ts` file. Requires `web.output: \"server\"` to be set in app config.',","+        'No longer required as of SDK 58 and has no effect. Remove this option from your app config.',","       default: 'false',","-      experimental: true,","+      deprecated: true,","     },","     {","       name: 'unstable_useServerDataLoaders',"],"additions":2,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/@expo/cli/CHANGELOG.md","lines":["@@ -6,6 +6,8 @@"," "," ### 🎉 New features"," ","+- Enable server middleware by default ([#49000](https://github.com/expo/expo/pull/49000) by [@hassankhan](https://github.com/hassankhan))","+"," ### 🐛 Bug fixes"," "," - Remove Expo Router compatibility checks for `@react-navigation` packages. ([#50176](https://github.com/expo/expo/pull/50176) by [@Ubax](https://github.com/Ubax))"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/@expo/cli/e2e/__tests__/export/server-middleware-matchers.test.ts","lines":["@@ -12,11 +12,6 @@ runExportSideEffects();"," describe('middleware matchers', () => {","   const configs = prepareServers([RUNTIME_EXPO_SERVE, RUNTIME_EXPO_START], {","     fixtureName: 'server-middleware-matcher-async',","-    export: {","-      env: {","-        E2E_ROUTER_SERVER_MIDDLEWARE: 'true',","-      },","-    },","   });"," ","   describe('pattern matching', () => {"],"additions":0,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/@expo/cli/e2e/__tests__/export/server-middleware.test.ts","lines":["@@ -1,14 +1,13 @@"," import fs from 'node:fs';"," import path from 'n